{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/kellner"},"metadata":{"extendedModule":"IvorTuning","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kellner"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"}],"externalID":"s:10IvorTuning0B6SystemPA2A15WellTemperamentVRszrlE7kellnerAEvpZ::SYNTHESIZED::s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","title":"kellner","roleHeading":"Type Property","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Self","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"WellTemperament","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]}},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Kellner (Herbert Anton Kellner, 1977)."}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/kellner"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kellner","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Five fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A, A→E, and B→F♯ — are each narrowed by ⅕ of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Pythagorean comma, equal to ⁵√(2¹⁴\/3⁷) ≈ 697.654 cents. The remaining seven"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fifths are pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Proposed by Kellner as a reconstruction of Bach’s own tuning, published in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Das Musikinstrument"}]},{"type":"text","text":" 26 (1977). The choice of five fifths and their positions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mirrors the structure of Werckmeister III while spreading the tempering more evenly."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"]]},"references":{"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament/kellner":{"title":"kellner","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kellner","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/kellner","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Kellner (Herbert Anton Kellner, 1977)."}],"conformance":{"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WellTemperament"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]},"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/kellner"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"WellTemperament","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tuning system in which all twelve keys are usable but have distinct tonal characters,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"achieved by distributing the Pythagorean comma unevenly around the circle of fifths."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"IvorTuning","abstract":[{"text":"Musical pitch, interval, and tuning system types.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning"}}}